{
  "raw": {
    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205617": {
      "title": "Program Manager, MBA & Executive MBA",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Program Manager, MBA & Executive MBA City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Program Manager, MBA & Executive MBA Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Program Manager, MBA & Executive MBA Category: Administrative Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Business and Management Locations: Seattle, WA Posted: Oct 7, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205617 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of National University. We serve students regionally, nationally, and globally, reaching across borders to impart knowledge and empower individuals. With a focus on adult learners and online students, we provide flexible, accessible programs tailored to meet the needs of the modern learner. Offering over 60 academic degree programs, we are committed to expanding our student's knowledge, skills, and possibilities. Our mission is deeply rooted in the belief that education can improve lives. We invite you to join us in our commitment to fostering community, promoting diversity, and providing an environment where every student can thrive and achieve their educational goals. Job Description: City University is seeking a Program Manager for our MBA and Executive MBA (EMBA) programs. This is an exciting opportunity to help shape graduate business programs that serve working professionals while bringing current business practices and industry perspectives into the student experience. Reporting to a Program Director, the Program Manager provides academic and program leadership across assigned MBA and EMBA program areas. The role combines curriculum and program development, faculty support, student engagement, teaching, and academic service. What You'll Do Support the development, review, and enhancement of MBA and EMBA programs, ensuring curriculum remains current, relevant, and aligned with CityU's academic model and accreditation standards. At the direction of the Program Director, serve as a subject matter expert and academic lead for assigned courses and program components. Teach three courses per year, or the equivalent within the role's compensation structure. Provide guidance and support to teaching faculty to promote excellence in teaching, learning, and student engagement. Support students throughout their academic journey through mentoring, coaching, and assistance with academic and course-related concerns. Monitor student engagement and progress, identify students who may be at risk, and develop proactive strategies to support retention and completion. Conduct regular student check-ins and create opportunities for student connection and engagement beyond the classroom. Contribute to academic governance through participation in councils, committees, and other institutional activities. Stay current with business, technology, and industry trends and incorporate relevant perspectives into curriculum and teaching. Build and participate in professional communities related to business and the role's areas of expertise. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below represent the knowledge, skills, and abilities required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Earned doctorate in business or a closely related business discipline. At least five years of professional experience in business or a related industry setting, preferably with experience in the Puget Sound business community. At least two years of experience working in or with international or culturally diverse business environments. At least two years of teaching experience, preferably including both in-person and online instruction. Knowledge of current and emerging technology trends and their impact on business. Ability to address academic concerns and support student retention and success. Ability to lead and collaborate effectively in a creative, fast-paced environment. Experience working effectively with virtual teams and in online environments. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal, and presentation skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with diverse students, faculty, staff, and external communities. Ability to represent CityU and the School of Business and Management professionally. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and learning management systems. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching graduate-level business courses, particularly MBA or EMBA courses. Experience working with adult learners and working professionals. Experience in curriculum development, program assessment, or academic program leadership. Experience working in higher education, particularly in an online or hybrid environment. Professional experience with a global or multinational organization. Additional Information: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here represent those that an employee must meet to perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to sit, talk, hear, and perform repetitive motions of the hands or wrists. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, grasp or handle, stoop or bend, and reach. Working Conditions: The working conditions described here represent those an employee encounters while performing this job's essential functions. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work is generally performed indoors in a typical office setting. Evening and weekend hours are required in this position. Travel, including overnight travel, may be required. Salary information: $85,000 - 90,000/ DOE Benefits information: We offer a comprehensive benefits package including paid holidays and paid time off; medical, dental, and vision insurance; health savings accounts (HSA/FSA); voluntary insurance; retirement benefits with employer matching; tuition benefits and other workplace perks such as flexible work schedules, anniversary programs and employee recognition programs, etc. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application includes the following: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Cover Letter Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. Responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account if you use the 'Help Desk' feature. A hiring manager will contact candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities, and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
    },
    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204638": {
      "title": "Program Director, Undergraduate Programs, School of Technology and Computing",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Program Director, Undergraduate Programs, School of Technology and Computing City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Program Director, Undergraduate Programs, School of Technology and Computing Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Program Director, Undergraduate Programs, School of Technology and Computing Category: Administrative Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Technology and Computing Locations: Seattle, WA Posted: Sep 9, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204638 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of National University. We serve students regionally, nationally, and globally, reaching across borders to impart knowledge and empower individuals. With a focus on adult learners and online students, we provide flexible, accessible programs tailored to meet the needs of the modern learner. Offering over 60 academic degree programs, we are committed to expanding our student's knowledge, skills, and possibilities. Our mission is deeply rooted in the belief that education can improve lives. We invite you to join us in our commitment to fostering community, promoting diversity, and providing an environment where every student can thrive and achieve their educational goals. Job Description: About the School of Technology & Computing The School of Technology & Computing (STC) brings together technology education and real-world industry experience. Our programs are designed for working professionals and career changers who want to build practical, relevant skills and apply them directly to today's technology landscape. STC offers undergraduate and graduate programs in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Data Science, and Cybersecurity, with flexible online and in-person learning options. What sets STC apart is our strong connection to the technology industry. Our students learn from faculty who bring current professional experience into the classroom, connecting academic concepts to the tools, challenges, and practices they encounter in the real world. We also welcome students entering technology from nontraditional backgrounds, with bridge and preparatory courses that help them build the foundation they need to succeed. We seek an innovative Program Director to lead undergraduate academic programs in Artificial Intelligence (AI), Computer Science (CS), Cybersecurity (CY), and Data Science (DS). In this pivotal leadership role, you will drive academic excellence in partnership with Seattle's thriving high-tech, maritime, healthcare, and related industries. You will spearhead the advancement of degree programs focused on AI, CS, CY, and DS, with special emphasis on Physical AI, Digital Twins, Cybersecurity in Operational Technology, and Autonomous Systems. Your work will help ensure CityU remains the top choice for students eager to tackle high-impact, real-world challenges. If you are passionate about transforming higher education through online, technology-driven innovation for lifelong learners, we encourage you to apply. Essential Duties and Responsibilities : Leads the planning, organization, direction, staffing, and oversight of assigned programs, encompassing curriculum development, assessment, ongoing review, and program enhancement. Aligns all program elements with current accreditation standards and requirements. Integrates the program curriculum with the CityU academic model, emphasizing real-world application and contemporary practices. Supervises, mentors, and evaluates academic staff and faculty to foster professional growth and teaching excellence. Models, encourages, and promotes scholarly engagement in teaching and learning. Leads orientation, training, and ongoing coaching for departmental faculty and administrative staff. Ensures timely and optimal nomination and assignment of faculty to courses. Advocates for student learning and engagement, proactively developing students into responsible, ethical, and self-directed professionals. Oversees student retention and graduation/completion rates and develops proactive interventions to support at-risk students. Monitors the fiscal health of assigned programs, including enrollment trends, headcount, and registration data. Maintains oversight of both quarterly and long-term course schedules, ensuring appropriate offerings for timely degree progress. Where applicable, supervises internship programs, establishing, approving, and supporting quality internship sites and professional partnerships with agencies and supervisors. Teaches or develops three courses per year (or equivalent) within compensation, ensuring required teaching assignments are met before engaging in additional teaching. Stays abreast of industry trends, standards, and best practices to ensure course content remains relevant and forward-looking. Actively participates in assigned committees and councils. Continues to contribute to applied research, publish scholarly articles on technology and computing, and earn industry certifications. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below represent the knowledge, skills, and abilities required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Undergraduate degree in STEM fields. An earned doctoral degree from an accredited institution in AI, CS, CY, DS, or a closely related discipline (Or we expect the candidate to receive their doctoral degree within 1 year) Demonstrated experience in higher education management and adult education, with at least three years of successful teaching?preferably in both in-person and online learning environments. Minimum of two years of progressively responsible experience in the technology industry. At least two publications in Artificial Intelligence (AI), Computer Science (CS), Cybersecurity (CY), or Data Science (DS) within the past three years. Proven ability to lead and manage teams in creative, innovative, virtual, and digital environments. Thorough understanding of the practitioner-faculty model and a strong commitment to delivering the highest quality educational experience in technology and computing. Ability to engage and communicate effectively with diverse students, faculty, staff, and external partners. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated expertise in research and/or teaching in Artificial Intelligence, Physical AI, Digital Twins, Cybersecurity (Information Technology or Operational Technology), Full-stack AI Development, or AI-Powered Software Engineering. Two or more AI-related publications within the past three years. Possession of industry certifications in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Cybersecurity, or Data Science. Experience effectively addressing student academic concerns and issues. Experience managing and leading virtual teams. Additional Information: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here represent those that an employee must meet to perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to sit, talk, hear, and perform repetitive motions of the hands or wrists. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, grasp or handle, stoop or bend, and reach. Working Conditions: The working conditions described here represent those an employee encounters while performing this job's essential functions. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work is generally performed indoors in a typical classroom/office setting or online. Maintaining an on-campus presence in Seattle at least two full days per week (Tuesdays or Thursdays during each academic quarter) is required. Attendance at occasional evening or weekend meetings/events may be required. Evening and weekend classes may be assigned. Travel, including overnight travel, may be required. Salary information: $105,000 - $115,000/year DOE Benefits information: We offer a comprehensive benefits package including paid holidays and paid time off; medical, dental, and vision insurance; health savings accounts (HSA/FSA); voluntary insurance; retirement benefits with employer matching; tuition benefits and other workplace perks such as flexible work schedules, anniversary programs and employee recognition programs, etc. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application includes the following: Completed Electronic Application Form CV Cover Letter Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. Responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account if you use the 'Help Desk' feature. A hiring manager will contact candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities, and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
    },
    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203756": {
      "title": "Program Director, Master of Arts in Counseling (MAC) Program",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Program Director, Master of Arts in Counseling (MAC) Program City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Program Director, Master of Arts in Counseling (MAC) Program Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Program Director, Master of Arts in Counseling (MAC) Program Category: Administrative Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Health and Social Sciences Locations: Seattle, WA Posted: Aug 14, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 203756 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of National University. We serve students regionally, nationally, and globally, reaching across borders to impart knowledge and empower individuals. With a focus on adult learners and online students, we provide flexible, accessible programs tailored to meet the needs of the modern learner. Offering over 60 academic degree programs, we are committed to expanding our student's knowledge, skills, and possibilities. Our mission is deeply rooted in the belief that education can improve lives. We invite you to join us in our commitment to fostering community, promoting diversity, and providing an environment where every student can thrive and achieve their educational goals. Job Description: Using a practitioner-scholar model, the Master of Arts in Counseling (MAC) program trains well-rounded clinical mental health counselors (CMHC) and professional school counselors (PSC) for the realities of day-to-day practice within a diverse world. The MAC program emphasizes practical application of theory, development of case conceptualization skills, ethical awareness, appreciation of diversity, and self-awareness. Students are introduced to a broad range of clinical issues through a breadth of coursework delivered by practitioner faculty. Supported clinical experiences focus on the delivery of clinical services and assist students to develop a coherent theoretical and ethical framework for practice. We are looking for an experienced professional to head our MAC program in the School of Health and Social Sciences. Job Summary: Program Directors are accountable for a quality student experience. Provide visionary leadership and management to ensure the success of the MAC program, including program design, curriculum development, assessment, and technology integration. Lead and manage academic staff, full-time faculty, and associate faculty. Foster student development and actively engage in educational governance. Essential Duties and Responsibilities : Program Management Lead the vision, strategy, and continuous improvement of the MAC program. Ensure academic excellence, program quality, and an exceptional student experience. Oversee curriculum assessment, development, and accreditation alignment. Internship Leadership Oversee student internship experiences and community partnerships. Develop and maintain high-quality internship sites and supervisor relationships. Support student success in field placement and professional development. Teaching & Student Success Teach up to three courses annually or the equivalent within compensation. Foster engaging, inclusive, and student-centered learning environments. Mentor students in becoming ethical, culturally responsive professionals. Faculty & Staff Leadership Recruit, supervise, develop, and evaluate faculty and academic staff. Promote a culture of collaboration, accountability, and professional growth. Provide coaching, mentoring, and performance leadership. Curriculum & Academic Excellence Ensure curriculum reflects current practice, accreditation standards, and industry needs. Lead ongoing program assessment and curriculum enhancement initiatives. Advance innovative and impactful learning experiences. Governance, Scholarship & Service Participate in university governance, councils, and committees. Promote faculty scholarship, professional development, and academic currency. Build community partnerships and represent the program within the profession. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below represent the knowledge, skills, and abilities required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. An earned doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Counseling or a related field, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program. Experience in higher education management and adult education, with a minimum of three years of proven experience in teaching, preferably in both in-class and online modes of educational delivery. Program development, administration, and leadership experience. Demonstrated experience leading and managing in a creative and fast-paced environment. Ability to work comfortably with and manage virtual teams. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal skills. Must relate to and communicate with diverse students, faculty, staff, and external communities. Ability to present an appropriate professional image. Proficiency with Microsoft Office products and learning management systems in support of quality teaching and learning. Additional Information: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here represent those that an employee must meet to perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to sit, talk, hear, and perform repetitive motions of the hands or wrists. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, grasp or handle, stoop or bend, and reach. Working Conditions: The working conditions described here represent those an employee encounters while performing this job's essential functions. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work is generally performed indoors in a typical office/classroom setting. Evening and weekend hours are required. Travel, including overnight travel, may be required. Salary information: $110,000 - $120,000/year Benefits information: We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes paid holidays, paid time off, health, dental, and vision insurance, healthcare spending or reimbursement accounts such as HSAs or FSAs, other voluntary insurance, retirement benefits and employer matching, tuition benefits, commuting/travel assistance, and other workplace perks. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application includes the following: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Cover Letter Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. Responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account if you use the 'Help Desk' feature. A hiring manager will contact candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities, and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
    },
    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205567": {
      "title": "Canada: Enrollment Advisor",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Canada: Enrollment Advisor City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Canada: Enrollment Advisor Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Canada: Enrollment Advisor Category: Canadian Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Canadian Operations Locations: Vancouver, British Columbia Posted: Oct 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205567 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of National University. We serve students regionally, nationally, and globally, reaching across borders to impart knowledge and empower individuals. With a focus on adult learners and online students, we provide flexible, accessible programs tailored to meet the needs of the modern learner. Offering over 60 academic degree programs, we are committed to expanding our student's knowledge, skills, and possibilities. Our mission is deeply rooted in the belief that education can improve lives. We invite you to join us in our commitment to fostering community, promoting diversity, and providing an environment where every student can thrive and achieve their educational goals. Job Description: Job Summary: The Enrollment Advisor serves as a primary point of contact for prospective and newly admitted students throughout the enrollment journey. This role builds relationships with prospective students, provides personalized admissions and program guidance, supports applicants through the application and admission process, and helps ensure a smooth transition into their first courses at CityU. The Enrollment Advisor works collaboratively with colleagues across Enrollment, Student Success, Marketing, Academic Affairs, and other university departments to provide a welcoming, responsive, and student-centered experience. The successful candidate will be comfortable working with a diverse student population, managing multiple priorities, and guiding students through complex information and processes with clarity and care. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Student Recruitment & Engagement Builds relationships with prospective students through timely and personalized outreach by phone, email, virtual meetings, and in-person interactions. Responds to inquiries and provides accurate information about CityU programs, admission requirements, tuition, financing options, and the enrollment process. Meets with prospective students to understand their educational goals and provide appropriate program and admissions guidance. Conducts timely follow-up with prospective students and maintains accurate records of interactions and enrollment activity in university systems. Participates in information sessions, recruitment activities, community events, and other outreach initiatives. Develops referral and community relationships that support student recruitment and enrollment. Admissions & Enrollment Guides prospective students through the application process, including required documentation, deadlines, and next steps. Reviews application materials for completeness and prepares application files for academic review. Participates in program-specific admissions interviews and processes as assigned. Communicates admission decisions and enrollment requirements clearly and professionally. Helps admitted students complete required steps toward enrollment and initial course registration. Identifies enrollment barriers and works with students and appropriate university departments to resolve issues. Student Support & University Engagement Supports newly admitted students as they transition from admission to enrollment and their first courses at CityU. Maintains accurate student records and serves as a liaison between students and appropriate university departments. Advocates for a positive student experience while following university policies and procedures. Represents CityU at community events, information sessions, and other university activities as assigned. Maintains current knowledge of CityU's academic programs, admissions policies, enrollment processes, and student financing options. Maintains knowledge of applicable privacy legislation, including provincial and federal requirements, and university policies governing student records and confidentiality. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skills, and/or abilities required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. At least two years of experience in admissions, enrollment, student advising, recruitment, customer service, higher education, or a related field. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain complex information clearly. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse cultural, racial, ethnic, socioeconomic, and professional backgrounds. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and handle sensitive student information appropriately. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and experience working with CRM, database, or student information systems. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in a Canadian post-secondary institution. Experience with admissions, enrollment advising, student recruitment, or student services. Experience working with adult learners, graduate students, or diverse student populations. Experience with PeopleSoft or another student information system. Familiarity with Canadian post-secondary admissions processes and privacy requirements. Experience with community outreach or professional relationship development. Additional Information: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here represent those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to sit, talk, hear and perform repetitive motions of the hand and/or wrists. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, grasp or handle, feel and reach. Working Conditions: The working conditions described here represent those an employee encounter while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work is generally performed indoors in a typical office setting. This is a hybrid position. Attendance at occasional evening or weekend meetings may be required. Location: Vancouver, British Columbia Salary information: CAD 55,000 - 65,000/year Benefits Information: We offer a comprehensive benefits package including paid holidays and paid time off; supplemental health plan; retirement savings plans with employer matching; tuition benefits; and other workplace perks such as flexible work schedules, selective commuter subsidy, employee recognition program, anniversary awards, etc. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application is one that includes: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Cover Letter Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. If you use the 'Help Desk' feature, responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account. Candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs will be contacted by a hiring manager. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
    },
    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204737": {
      "title": "Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Psychology Program, Virtual Campus",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Psychology Program, Virtual Campus City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Psychology Program, Virtual Campus Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Psychology Program, Virtual Campus Category: Canadian Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Health and Social Sciences Locations: Virtual, Alberta Posted: Sep 11, 2026 Closes: Sep 30, 2027 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Part-time Position ID: 204737 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of National University. We serve students regionally, nationally, and globally, reaching across borders to impart knowledge and empower individuals. With a focus on adult learners and online students, we provide flexible, accessible programs tailored to meet the needs of the modern learner. Offering over 60 academic degree programs, we are committed to expanding our student's knowledge, skills, and possibilities. Our mission is deeply rooted in the belief that education can improve lives. We invite you to join us in our commitment to fostering community, promoting diversity, and providing an environment where every student can thrive and achieve their educational goals. Job Description: City University of Seattle in Canada is seeking qualified part-time Associate Faculty to teach in the School of Health and Social Sciences' Master of Counselling Psychology Program at our Virtual Campus. The Virtual Campus delivers entirely online, bringing together students and faculty from across Canada. We are seeking experienced, registered psychologists with expertise in counselling psychology who are passionate about graduate-level teaching, student development, and professional practice. Associate Faculty members contribute not only through high-quality teaching, but also through collaboration and ongoing engagement with colleagues, students, and the broader learning and professional community. Faculty may have opportunities to contribute to program initiatives, student learning and development, professional engagement, and other activities that support the MC program community. Teaching Opportunities Teaching opportunities may be available across a range of clinically and non-clinically focused courses. Courses may include: Assessment in Counselling Psychology Systemic Theory: Diversity and Cultural Psychology Professional Ethics and Law Psychopathology and Psychopharmacology Research Methods and Statistics Counselling Psychology Theory Psychology of Addictions Psychology of Trauma and Interpersonal Violence Group Counselling Psychology Courses are delivered online using Zoom and Brightspace. Teaching may include synchronous weekday, evening, or weekend sessions. Some courses may incorporate asynchronous or mixed-mode learning activities. Faculty Responsibilities Associate Faculty members are expected to: Deliver high-quality, engaging instruction that supports student learning and professional development. Foster an inclusive learning environment that supports student success and development. Connect academic learning with current professional practice in counselling psychology. Maintain current professional knowledge, practice, and standards in the field. Collaborate with faculty, academic leadership, and professional staff to support a strong and connected learning community. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Registration as a psychologist with the applicable regulatory body in a Canadian jurisdiction. A master's degree from an accredited institution is required; a doctoral degree is preferred. The terminal degree must include \"psychology\" in the degree title. A minimum of three years of professional experience following registration; five years is preferred. Demonstrated professional experience and expertise relevant to counselling psychology and the courses the faculty member is qualified to teach. Prior teaching experience at the post-secondary level is an asset. Demonstrated ability to support students with academic-related issues and concerns in ways that promote learning and student success. Demonstrated commitment to culturally responsive and inclusive teaching practices and the ability to work effectively with diverse student populations. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal, and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to connect professional practice with academic learning and adult learning principles. Demonstrated ability and willingness to collaborate with faculty, academic leadership, and professional staff and to maintain ongoing engagement with the program community. Ability to work effectively with culturally diverse students, faculty, and staff in a collaborative environment. Proficiency with learning management systems and technology used to support effective virtual teaching, including Zoom and Brightspace. Ability to present a professional and collegial presence on behalf of the School of Health and Social Sciences and City University of Seattle. Additional Information: Work Environment This is a virtual teaching position. Faculty are expected to have a suitable workspace, personal computer, reliable high-speed internet connection, and the technology necessary to support effective online teaching. Evening and weekend teaching may be required depending on course scheduling and program needs. Appointment Part-time, course-by-course appointments are made based on program needs, course availability, enrollment, and faculty qualifications. Compensation Compensation is determined based on course level, faculty qualifications and experience, registration, and course credit hours. About the Master of Counselling Program To learn more about City University of Seattle's Master of Counselling Psychology program, Virtual Campus, visit https://cityuniversity.ca/virtual-mc/. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application is one that includes: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Cover Letter Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. If you use the 'Help Desk' feature, responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account. Candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs will be contacted by a hiring manager. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
    },
    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203261": {
      "title": "Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Program, Victoria Campus",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Program, Victoria Campus City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Program, Victoria Campus Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Program, Victoria Campus Category: Canadian Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Health and Social Sciences Locations: Victoria, British Columbia Posted: Jul 31, 2026 Closes: Jun 30, 2027 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Part-time Position ID: 203261 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of National University. We serve students regionally, nationally, and globally, reaching across borders to impart knowledge and empower individuals. With a focus on adult learners and online students, we provide flexible, accessible programs tailored to meet the needs of the modern learner. Offering over 60 academic degree programs, we are committed to expanding our student's knowledge, skills, and possibilities. Our mission is deeply rooted in the belief that education can improve lives. We invite you to join us in our commitment to fostering community, promoting diversity, and providing an environment where every student can thrive and achieve their educational goals. Job Description: City University of Seattle in Canada's Master of Counselling (MC) program in Victoria, BC, is seeking experienced Associate Faculty to join a small, dedicated, and innovative team of educators. The Victoria campus is located on the ancestral and unceded territories of the Lekwungen-speaking peoples, including the Esquimalt, Songhees, and W_SáNEC First Nations . We are seeking counselling professionals who bring current clinical experience, strong teaching experience with adult learners, and expertise in a counselling-related practice area . Associate Faculty teach graduate-level courses on a course-by-course basis and play an important role in preparing future counselling professionals for clinical practice. About the Role Associate Faculty teach courses related to core counselling proficiencies, assessment, counselling skills, clinical practice, and other areas of the counselling field. Course assignments are based on program needs and faculty expertise; teaching assignments are not guaranteed from term to term or from academic year to academic year. Successful Associate Faculty may have opportunities to take on additional or longer-term teaching responsibilities based on program needs, performance, and experience. Examples of courses may include: Couples Counselling Group Counselling Psychopathology and Psychopharmacology Clinical Supervision Testing and Assessment Research Methods and Statistics Counselling Research Capstone Teaching Responsibilities Associate Faculty are expected to: Deliver high-quality, engaging instruction that supports graduate student learning. Connect academic theory, research, and clinical practice. Foster student development and professional growth. Maintain currency in their professional field and area of teaching. Participate in the academic community and work collaboratively with faculty and program leadership. Use appropriate teaching technologies and Learning Management Systems to support effective learning. Requirements: What You'll Bring We are particularly interested in candidates who have demonstrated success as both counselling professionals and educators . Required Qualifications Master's degree or doctoral degree in counselling, psychology, clinical social work, or a closely related field. Current registration with an appropriate professional regulatory body. At least five years of clinical practice after registration, plus meaningful professional experience in the counselling field. At least two years of experience providing instruction to adult learners in classroom and/or online settings. Demonstrated success and effectiveness as an instructor, educator, or facilitator. Demonstrated ability to bridge counselling theory and clinical practice in a graduate-level learning environment. Current knowledge and professional experience in at least one area relevant to counselling practice. Ability to work effectively within an established curriculum and course framework. Strong oral, written, interpersonal, and presentation skills. Ability to create an engaging learning environment for a diverse population of graduate students. Cultural competence and demonstrated ability to work respectfully with diverse students, faculty, and communities. Additional Qualifications and Skills Experience teaching in a graduate counselling or related program is an asset. Doctoral degree is preferred. Familiarity with diverse pedagogical approaches and adult learning principles. Experience teaching both in-person and online courses is an asset. Comfort with digital teaching environments, including Learning Management Systems, presentation technology, and audiovisual equipment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and other technology used to support teaching and learning. Ability to support students with academic-related questions and concerns and contribute to student success and retention. Commitment to ongoing professional development and maintaining currency in the counselling profession. Additional Information: Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion City University of Seattle in Canada is committed to fostering a learning environment that reflects and respects the diversity of the communities we serve. We welcome applicants who bring diverse perspectives, experiences, identities, and approaches to counselling education, including Indigenous Peoples, First Nations, Inuit, and Métis applicants . Applicants must demonstrate their capacity to work collaboratively and respectfully within a diverse community of learners and educators. Work Environment and Schedule Location: Victoria, British Columbia Delivery: In-person and mixed-mode Courses may be scheduled on weekdays, evenings, or weekends depending on program and student needs. A personal computer and reliable internet connection are required. Teaching assignments are made based on program needs and are not guaranteed from term to term. Compensation CAD 3,300 - 5,500 per course, depending on course level, professional registration, and experience. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application is one that includes: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Cover Letter Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. If you use the 'Help Desk' feature, responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account. Candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs will be contacted by a hiring manager. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
    },
    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203260": {
      "title": "Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Program, Edmonton Campus",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Program, Edmonton Campus City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Program, Edmonton Campus Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Canada: Associate Faculty, Master of Counselling Program, Edmonton Campus Category: Canadian Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Health and Social Sciences Locations: Edmonton, Alberta Posted: Jul 31, 2026 Closes: Jun 30, 2027 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Part-time Position ID: 203260 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of National University. We serve students regionally, nationally, and globally, reaching across borders to impart knowledge and empower individuals. With a focus on adult learners and online students, we provide flexible, accessible programs tailored to meet the needs of the modern learner. Offering over 60 academic degree programs, we are committed to expanding our student's knowledge, skills, and possibilities. Our mission is deeply rooted in the belief that education can improve lives. We invite you to join us in our commitment to fostering community, promoting diversity, and providing an environment where every student can thrive and achieve their educational goals. Job Description: City University of Seattle in Canada is seeking qualified part-time Associate Faculty members for the School of Health and Social Sciences in the Master of Counseling Program, Edmonton Campus. Ideal candidates are qualified, registered psychologists or counselling and psychology professionals with a graduate degree in psychology (doctoral-level preferred), with knowledge and experience in post-secondary education, delivery, and instruction. The MC program's teaching opportunities include various clinically and non-clinically focused courses. These course offerings may include Assessment in Counselling Psychology, Systemic Theory: Diversity and Cultural Psychology, Professional Ethics and Law, Psychopathology and Psychopharmacology, Research Methods and Statistics, Counselling Psychology Theory, Psychology of Addictions, Psychology of Trauma and Interpersonal Violence, and Group Counselling Psychology. Courses are delivered either in person or in mixed mode. To learn more about the MC program, visit our website at https://www.cityuniversity.ca/academics/graduate-programs/master-counselling/ Part-time Teaching Faculty at CityU has three key responsibilities: Striving for excellence in teaching and learning. Fostering student development. Maintaining currency in their profession. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below represent the knowledge, skills, and abilities required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. A Registered psychologist or mental health professional with a doctoral degree (preferred) or master's in psychology. A minimum of 5 years post-registration clinical experience. Registration with a regulatory body consistent with the field of practice. Prior teaching experience is an asset. Skills in addressing student academic-related issues and concerns in support of retention and student success. Culturally competent to serve a diverse student and faculty body. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to provide a learning experience that links application with formal learning and adult learning theory. Ability to work in a team-oriented system and deal effectively with professional staff, faculty, and culturally diverse students. Ability to present a professional image for the school and City University of Seattle. Proficiency with Microsoft Office products and learning management systems in support of quality teaching and learning. Personal computer, video camera, and access to reliable internet. Additional Information: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here represent those that an employee must meet to perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, sit, talk, hear, and perform repetitive motions of the hands or wrists. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, grasp or handle, stoop or bend, and reach. Working Conditions: The working conditions described here represent those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work is generally performed indoors in a typical office and classroom setting. Weekend hours may be required depending on class availability. Personal computer, video camera, and reliable internet prerequisites. Term : Academic year 2026 - 2027 Salary : Associate Faculty salary is based on the course level, faculty registration and experience, and the number of course credits (1-5). Delivery Mode: In-person and mixed mode. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application includes: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Cover Letter Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. Responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account if you use the 'Help Desk' feature. A hiring manager will contact candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities, and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
    },
    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205748": {
      "title": "Full-Time Teaching Faculty, MA in Marriage and Family Therapy Program",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Full-Time Teaching Faculty, MA in Marriage and Family Therapy Program City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Full-Time Teaching Faculty, MA in Marriage and Family Therapy Program Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Full-Time Teaching Faculty, MA in Marriage and Family Therapy Program Category: Full-time Teaching Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Health and Social Science Locations: Seattle, WA Posted: Oct 13, 2026 Closes: Oct 27, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Position ID: 205748 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of National University. We serve students regionally, nationally, and globally, reaching across borders to impart knowledge and empower individuals. With a focus on adult learners and online students, we provide flexible, accessible programs tailored to meet the needs of the modern learner. Offering over 60 academic degree programs, we are committed to expanding our student's knowledge, skills, and possibilities. Our mission is deeply rooted in the belief that education can improve lives. We invite you to join us in our commitment to fostering community, promoting diversity, and providing an environment where every student can thrive and achieve their educational goals. Job Description: City University of Seattle invites applications for a Full-Time Teaching Faculty position in the Master of Arts in Marriage and Family Therapy (MFT) program. In addition to teaching graduate-level courses, this position plays a key role in coordinating student clinical training, including practicum and internship experiences, clinical placements, supervision, and competency development. Working collaboratively with program leadership and faculty, the successful candidate will support students' clinical readiness, maintain relationships with clinical placement sites and supervisors, and contribute to program assessment and accreditation activities. Teaching responsibilities may be adjusted annually based on the workload associated with clinical training coordination. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Coordinate student clinical training processes, including practicum and internship placements, clinical readiness, and ongoing student progress. Develop and maintain relationships with clinical placement sites and clinical supervisors to support quality training experiences. Monitor student clinical hours, supervision requirements, and clinical competency development. Contribute to the assessment of student learning, clinical outcomes, and program effectiveness. Support program accreditation and continuous improvement activities, including compliance with Commission on Accreditation for Marriage and Family Therapy Education (COAMFTE) standards, reporting, and self-study preparation. Teach graduate-level MFT courses and advise and mentor students. Participate in admissions, student orientation, curriculum review, and faculty meetings. Promote ethical, systemic, and culturally responsive clinical practice. Collaborate with program leadership and faculty to develop and improve clinical training policies, procedures, and resources. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below represent the knowledge, skills, and abilities required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Master's or doctoral degree in Marriage and Family Therapy or a related field. Current Washington State Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT) credential, or eligibility to meet applicable university requirements. At least two years of graduate-level teaching experience. At least three years of clinical experience working with individuals, couples, and families. Demonstrated knowledge of clinical training, supervision practices, student assessment, and COAMFTE standards. Preferred Qualifications PhD, DMFT, or EdD. AAMFT Approved Supervisor status or status as an Approved Supervisor Candidate. Experience coordinating practicum, internship, clinical placement, or other clinical education activities. Experience in a COAMFTE-accredited or accreditation-seeking MFT program. Experience with program assessment, accreditation reporting, and faculty leadership. Additional Information: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here represent those that an employee must meet to perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to sit, talk, hear, and perform repetitive motions of the hands or wrists. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, grasp or handle, stoop or bend, and reach. Working Conditions: The working conditions described here represent those an employee encounters while performing this job's essential functions. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work is generally performed indoors in a typical office setting. Evening and weekend hours are required in this position. Travel, including overnight travel, may be required. Salary information: $81,000 - 85,000/ year Benefits information: We offer a comprehensive benefits package including paid holidays and paid time off; medical, dental, and vision insurance; health savings accounts (HSA/FSA); voluntary insurance; retirement benefits with employer matching; tuition benefits and other workplace perks such as flexible work schedules, anniversary programs and employee recognition programs, etc. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application includes the following: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Cover Letter Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. Responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account if you use the 'Help Desk' feature. A hiring manager will contact candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities, and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
    },
    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=195044": {
      "title": "Part-Time Teaching Faculty, Mexico Programs",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Part-Time Teaching Faculty, Mexico Programs City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Teaching Faculty, Mexico Programs Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Teaching Faculty, Mexico Programs Category: Part-Time Teaching Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Mexico Program Locations: Various, Other Posted: Nov 21, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 195044 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of the National University System. We are dedicated to providing accessible, achievable higher education to adult learners. As a pioneer in digital learning, we have been delivering online education for over 40 years. CityU is ranked by the U.S. News & World Report among the top for online bachelor's degree programs and among the top online programs for veterans in the U.S. CityU prides itself on having a completion rate of twice the national average, according to data from the Chronicle of Higher Education. CityU has over 20 locations in the Northwest and worldwide. Many of our degree, certificate, and endorsement programs are offered online, in-person, mixed-mode, and in performance-based formats. Aside from its flagship campus and headquarters in Seattle, CityU offers programs in Canada, China, the Czech Republic, Mexico, Slovakia, Switzerland, and Vietnam. Job Description: Teach Business. Experience Mexico. Shape the World. Take a working vacation and experience the rich cultural tapestry of Mexico. Home to vibrant cities, welcoming communities, and breathtaking landscapes from Tamaulipas to Mexico City. We are seeking instructors to teach English-language business and technology courses at the doctoral, graduate, and undergraduate levels with our partner institutions, Universidad Autónoma de Tamaulipas and Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México. Join a team of dedicated professionals who teach in City University of Seattle's international partner programs and bring your expertise abroad. Share the knowledge and skills you've honed with students in English-language programs at our partner universities. Successful candidates will bring strong professional experience and academic credentials to create highly engaging learning experiences, contributing to an integrated program that offers a global perspective on business and technology. CityU School of Business and Management is seeking qualified faculty at the Undergraduate, Graduate, and Doctoral levels in the following areas: Finance Accounting Marketing Economics Project Management Supply Chain Data Analytics Artificial Intelligence (Business-related) Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below represent the knowledge, skills, and abilities required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Master's degree in a business field (doctorate preferred). Minimum two years of professional experience in relevant business areas. Teaching experience in business. Valid U.S. passport or Green Card with no travel restrictions. Ability to travel internationally twice during the 10-week quarter (weekend travel). Professional, polished representation of City University of Seattle. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and learning management systems. Strong English communication and interpersonal skills; ability to work with diverse groups. Understanding of Mexican students' needs, learning styles, and perspectives. Knowledge of and positive attitude toward Mexican culture. Additional Information: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here represent those that an employee must meet to perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, sit, talk, hear, and perform repetitive motions of the hands or wrists. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, grasp or handle, stoop or bend, and reach. Working Conditions: The working conditions described here represent those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work is generally performed indoors in a typical office setting. Remote work may be needed. Teaching assignments occur during our standard 10-week academic quarters. International travel required. Support and Compensation: CityU provides the following each time the instructor is invited to teach a course session: Visa sponsorship A $2,500-$3,000 fixed fee, with travel expenses fully covered. Program support for instructional development and teaching administration. Additional information regarding logistics will be provided during interviews and onboarding. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application includes the following: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Cover letter describing course(s) you feel most qualified to teach, qualifications for the courses, and reasons for interest in the work Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. Responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account if you use the 'Help Desk' feature. A hiring manager will contact candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities, and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
    },
