      "title": "Part-Time Teaching Faculty, Vietnam Programs",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Part-Time Teaching Faculty, Vietnam Programs City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Teaching Faculty, Vietnam Programs Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Teaching Faculty, Vietnam Programs Category: Part-Time Teaching Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Vietnam Program Locations: Various, Other Posted: Nov 21, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 195043 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of the National University System. We are dedicated to providing accessible, achievable higher education to adult learners. As a pioneer in digital learning, we have been delivering online education for over 40 years. CityU is ranked by the U.S. News & World Report among the top for online bachelor's degree programs and among the top online programs for veterans in the U.S. CityU prides itself on having a completion rate of twice the national average, according to data from the Chronicle of Higher Education. CityU has over 20 locations in the Northwest and worldwide. Many of our degree, certificate, and endorsement programs are offered online, in-person, mixed-mode, and in performance-based formats. Aside from its flagship campus and headquarters in Seattle, CityU offers programs in Canada, China, the Czech Republic, Mexico, Slovakia, Switzerland, and Vietnam. Job Description: Transform Futures. Share Your Expertise in Vietnam. Take a working vacation and experience the excitement of teaching in Vietnam, a dynamic, fast-growing economy known for its vibrant culture, welcoming communities, and stunning landscapes stretching from Hanoi to the Mekong Delta.  We are seeking instructors to teach English-language business and technology courses at the doctoral, graduate, and undergraduate levels with our partner institutions, The Banking Academy of Vietnam (BAV), Center of International Education- Da Nang University of Economics (DUE), and The University of Economics in Ho Chi Minh City (UEH). Join a team of fellow professionals who teach in City University of Seattle's partner programs abroad and take your expertise on the road. Share the discipline and skill set you've developed in person with students in the English-language programs at our partner institutions. Successful candidates will bring strong experience and academic credentials to create highly engaging student experiences, delivering their part of an integrated partner program that reflects an international perspective on business and technology. CityU School of Business and Management is seeking qualified faculty at the Undergraduate, Graduate, and Doctoral levels in the following areas: Finance Accounting Marketing Economics Project Management Supply Chain Data Analytics Artificial Intelligence (Business-related) Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below represent the knowledge, skills, and abilities required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. A master's degree in a business-related field (doctorate preferred). At least two years of professional experience in one or more relevant business areas. Proven instructional experience in the business field and a commitment to student success. A valid U.S. passport or Green Card with no travel restrictions. The confidence and polish to represent City University of Seattle at the highest level. Strong skills in Microsoft Office and learning management systems to deliver dynamic, high-quality learning. Excellent English writing and speaking abilities, plus the interpersonal skills to connect with diverse students, faculty, and staff. An understanding of the needs, interests, and learning styles of Vietnamese students. Familiarity with Vietnamese culture and a positive, respectful attitude toward the Vietnamese community. A vibrant, professional presence that reflects the university's values and commitment to global education Additional Information: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here represent those that an employee must meet to perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, sit, talk, hear, and perform repetitive motions of the hands or wrists. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, grasp or handle, stoop or bend, and reach. Working Conditions: The working conditions described here represent those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work is generally performed indoors in a typical office setting. Remote work may be needed. Weekend hours may be required depending on class availability. International travel required. Teaching assignments occur during our standard 10-week academic quarters. Support and Compensation: CityU provides the following each time the instructor is invited to teach a course session: Visa sponsorship A $2,500-$3,000 fixed fee, with all travel expenses fully covered. Program support for instructional development and teaching administration. Additional information regarding logistics will be provided during interviews and onboarding. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application includes the following: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Cover letter describing course(s) you feel most qualified to teach, qualifications for the courses, and reasons for interest in the work Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. Responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account if you use the 'Help Desk' feature. A hiring manager will contact candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities, and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
