er instructional hour) or $1000 for teaching a course in person ($50 per instructional hour) Classes are offered between 9:00 a.m. and 9:00 p.m., with most World Language courses meeting 6:30-8:30 p.m. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, sit, talk, hear, and perform repetitive motions of the hands or wrists. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, grasp or handle, stoop or bend, and reach. Working Conditions: The working conditions described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Work is generally performed indoors in a typical office and classroom setting. Weekend hours may be required depending on class availability Location: On-site, hybrid, and online; based in Seattle. Application Instructions: Join Our Team If you're passionate about language education and enjoy helping adult learners build practical communication skills and cultural understanding, we'd love to hear from you. Application Instructions City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application is one that includes: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Cover Letter Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. If you use the 'Help Desk' feature, responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account. Candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs will be contacted by a hiring manager. Once the position i