    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203755": {
      "title": "Student Assistant, Site Operations",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: Student Assistant, Site Operations City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: Student Assistant, Site Operations Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Student Assistant, Site Operations Category: Student Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Site Operations Locations: Seattle, WA Posted: Aug 14, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 203755 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of the National University. We serve students regionally, nationally, and globally, reaching across borders to impart knowledge and empower individuals. With a focus on adult learners and online students, we provide flexible, accessible programs tailored to meet the needs of the modern learner. Offering over 60 academic degree programs, we are committed to expanding our students' knowledge, skills, and possibilities. Our mission is deeply rooted in the belief that education can improve lives. We invite you to join us in our commitment to fostering community, promoting diversity, and providing an environment where every student can thrive and achieve their educational goals. Job Description: All students are welcome to apply, but we prefer students at least one year away from completing their studies to avoid quick turnovers. Job Summary: Provides operational support for all student services, classrooms, and staffing needs during daily operation. Serves as the first point of contact for customer service needs at the front desk, on the phone, and in the classrooms. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Work closely with site staff to ensure effective and efficient site operations. Work cooperatively with Enrollment, Academics, the Business Office, Facilities, and other departments to resolve student or site issues promptly and professionally. Work with site staff to coordinate needs for local events. Work with the IT department to gain basic knowledge to help with students' computer or network issues. Provide front desk coverage and customer service to students, instructors, and property management with other support staff. Coordinate classroom availability and scheduling, ensuring buildings and classrooms are open on time and equipment is operational and available. Ensure that classrooms are properly cleaned after all classes and events. Assist with exam proctoring if needed. Perform administrative tasks, including word processing, spreadsheet or database creation and maintenance, filing, supplies ordering, mailing, in-house distribution, composing reports and correspondence, etc. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Enrollment in a City University degree program is required. Minimum of one year of office admin or customer service experience. Must demonstrate a high level of customer service, attention to detail, and organizational and problem-solving ability. Ability to perform job duties with minimal supervision, effectively prioritize work, multi-task, and adjust to changing workloads and deadlines. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret documents, such as safety rules, operating instructions, and procedure manuals. Ability to write routine correspondence. Ability to communicate effectively with diverse student, staff, and faculty populations. Proficiency with MS Office products. Additional Information: Physical Demands: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, stoop or bend, talk, reach, use repetitive motion of hands/wrists, sit, grasp or handle, hear, feel, and walk. The employee will regularly use cleaning products such as disinfectants, whiteboard cleaner, etc. The employee is occasionally required to use repetitive motion of the feet and kneel. The employee must frequently lift, carry, push, or pull up to 50 pounds. Working Conditions: Work is generally performed indoors in a typical office/front desk setting. Attendance on evenings or weekends may be required. Salary information: This is a part-time (19.5 hours per week) student position. This position pays a minimum wage of $21.30/hour. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application includes: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. Responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account if you use the 'Help Desk' feature. A hiring manager will contact candidates with qualifications and experience most aligned with current needs. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities, and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
    },
    "https://cityu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203174": {
      "title": "International Student Ambassador, International Recruitment",
      "description": "City University of Seattle\nJob Posting: International Student Ambassador, International Recruitment City University of Seattle \n\tJob Posting: International Student Ambassador, International Recruitment Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details International Student Ambassador, International Recruitment Category: Student Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: International Student Services Locations: Seattle, WA Posted: Jul 29, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 203174 Share About City University of Seattle: City University of Seattle (CityU) is a distinguished and comprehensive private nonprofit university and an affiliate of the National University. We serve students regionally, nationally, and globally, reaching across borders to impart knowledge and empower individuals. With a focus on adult learners and online students, we provide flexible, accessible programs tailored to meet the needs of the modern learner. Offering over 60 academic degree programs, we are committed to expanding our student's knowledge, skills, and possibilities. Our mission is deeply rooted in the belief that education can improve lives. We invite you to join us in our commitment to fostering community, promoting diversity, and providing an environment where every student can thrive and achieve their educational goals. Job Description: All students are welcome to apply, but we prefer students at least one year away from completing their studies at CityU to avoid quick turnovers. Job Summary: Provides administrative and peer support for international student recruitment. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Act as a resource for new and current international students, providing support, guidance, and information about campus resources, policies, and student life. Assist with the onboarding process, such as orientation programs, campus tours, and settling into university life. Help international students integrate into the campus community through engagement activities and social events. Respond to emails, inquiries, and concerns from prospective or current international students. Help plan and execute events such as welcome luncheons and any other events on campus. Offer peer-to-peer guidance to help students overcome cultural, academic, and social challenges. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Must be a current CityU student in good academic standing, typically with an international background or strong intercultural experience. Proficient in English, with additional language skills considered an asset. An understanding of and respect for diverse cultures and perspectives. Familiar with campus resources, programs, and student services. Ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines. Comfortable engaging with diverse groups and individuals. Preferred Skills: Leadership and mentoring skills. Event planning and organizational experience. Intercultural communication and problem-solving abilities. Networking and public speaking skills. Additional Information: Physical Demands: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, stoop or bend, talk, reach, use repetitive motion of hands/wrists, sit, grasp or handle, hear, feel, and walk. The employee must occasionally lift, carry, push, or pull up to 20 pounds. Working Conditions: Work is generally performed indoors in a typical office setting. Hours: This is a part-time (11 hours per week) student position. Salary: This position pays a minimum wage of $21.30 per hour. Application Instructions: City University of Seattle accepts applications through this online process only. For consideration, please submit a complete application packet. A complete application includes: Completed Electronic Application Form Resume Once you have created a profile, please remember to record your password. Responses will be sent to your Interview Exchange account if you use the 'Help Desk' feature. A hiring manager will contact candidates whose qualifications and experience most align with our current needs. Once the position is filled, you will see a status update in your account profile. If you encounter technical problems while applying for a position, please use the 'Help Desk' feature in your Interview Exchange account to submit the issue to technical support. For non-technical issues or questions, please email employment@cityu.edu. City University of Seattle is an equal opportunity employer and is continuously working to build a diverse faculty and staff. City University strongly encourages inquiries from all qualified individuals interested in becoming part of the CityU team, including women, Aboriginal peoples, persons with disabilities, and members of visible minorities. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation City University of Seattle 521 Wall St., Suite 100 Seattle, WA 98121"
